# s3-05 core wire (CORE-WIRE-G2)

## native/core/crates/mixdog-tools/src/desktop/mod.rs
After the line `mod computer_gnome;` (alphabetical, before `mod computer_internal_windows;`) add:
    pub mod computer_history;

## Cargo.toml / workspace members / [dependencies]
None. The module uses only what mixdog-tools already depends on (serde_json, sha2, uuid v4, chrono, url, mixdog-js,
mixdog-core-api) and tempfile (dev-dependency) for its tests. No new workspace edge, no Cargo.lock change.

## compose call
None. The module is a library of three types; nothing registers.

## Consumers (not this task)
- `ProcessComputerBackend` in computer_backend.rs answers `"list_history"` with `unsupported("list kind=\"history\" needs the desktop host's action ledger")`.
  The task that wires the backend replaces it with
  `RunLog::new(&data_dir).history(&session_id, history_limit(command.get("limit")))` (the reply text is that Value as JSON,
  exactly `{"history":[...],"returned":n}`), and appends after each command with
  `RunLog::append(session, run_record(&command, elapsed_ms, reply.as_ref()))` and
  `FailureBundles::record(session, &diagnostic_input)`; the data dir is `ComputerSettings.data_dir`.
- SERVICE_PENDING in compose_flip.rs: no protocol method is registered by this task, so no name is removed.
